/* Curated offline knowledge base for Atelier Doubt Assistant. No network AI, API key or model download. */
window.ATELIER_DOUBT_KB = {"version":1,"entries":[{"id":"start-drawing","aliases":["how do i start drawing","beginner drawing","start learning art","drawing start kaise karu","draw karna kaise shuru","i am a beginner","new to drawing"],"keywords":["beginner","start","starting","basics","beginner","shuru","seekhna","drawing","art"],"en":"Start with simple, repeatable fundamentals: confident lines, ellipses, basic shapes, then turn those shapes into 3D forms. Use ordinary paper and one pencil; you do not need expensive supplies. Practise for a short, focused session and date your pages so you can compare progress.","hi":"Shuruaat simple fundamentals se karo: confident lines, ellipses, basic shapes, phir unhe 3D forms mein badlo. Ek pencil aur normal paper kaafi hain; expensive supplies ki zaroorat nahi. Roz thodi focused practice karo aur pages par date likho, taaki progress compare kar sako.","modules":["m1","m2","m4","m5","m6","m7"]},{"id":"talent","aliases":["do i need talent","am i talented","can anyone learn drawing","born artist","talent matters","drawing talent","talent zaroori"],"keywords":["talent","learn","anyone","born","natural","gifted","skill","practice"],"en":"Drawing is a learnable skill, not a fixed talent test. Improvement comes from deliberate practice: choose one specific problem, practise it with focus, then review what changed. Compare your current work with your own earlier work, not a professional’s finished portfolio.","hi":"Drawing ek seekhi ja sakne wali skill hai, fixed talent test nahi. Improvement deliberate practice se aati hai: ek specific problem chuno, focus ke saath practise karo, phir dekho kya improve hua. Apne aaj ke kaam ko apne purane kaam se compare karo, kisi professional ke portfolio se nahi.","modules":["m1","m4"]},{"id":"materials","aliases":["what pencil should i use","which pencil","drawing materials","art supplies","what tools do i need","pencil grade","hb 2b","kaunsi pencil","kya saman chahiye"],"keywords":["pencil","materials","tools","supplies","hb","2b","eraser","paper","samagri"],"en":"For the early fundamentals, an HB or 2B pencil, a basic eraser, a sharpener and plain paper are enough. Save expensive sketchbook paper for work you want to keep. Learn pressure control before buying a large pencil set.","hi":"Shuruaati fundamentals ke liye HB ya 2B pencil, basic eraser, sharpener aur normal paper kaafi hain. Achha sketchbook paper un drawings ke liye bachao jinhe sambhal kar rakhna hai. Bada pencil set kharidne se pehle pressure control seekho.","modules":["m2"]},{"id":"grip","aliases":["how to hold pencil","pencil grip","overhand grip","writing grip","pencil kaise pakde","grip kaise"],"keywords":["grip","hold","pencil","overhand","tripod","writing","pakad"],"en":"Use a writing/tripod grip for small controlled details. Use an overhand grip for longer, looser strokes and broad construction. Keep the grip relaxed; let the shoulder and elbow help with longer marks instead of forcing every movement from the fingers.","hi":"Chhoti details ke liye writing/tripod grip use karo. Lambi, loose lines aur broad construction ke liye overhand grip better hai. Pencil ko relaxed pakdo; lambi lines mein sirf fingers nahi, shoulder aur elbow ko bhi move karne do.","modules":["m3"]},{"id":"lines","aliases":["how to draw straight lines","line confidence","wobbly lines","shaky lines","line practice","seedhi line","line control"],"keywords":["line","lines","straight","ghosting","wobbly","shaky","stroke","seedhi","lakir"],"en":"Use the ghosting method: mark the start and end points, rehearse the movement above the page, then make one committed stroke. Draw from the shoulder for longer lines. Do not repeatedly scratch over a line to rescue it.","hi":"Ghosting method use karo: start aur end points mark karo, page ke upar movement rehearse karo, phir ek confident stroke lagao. Lambi lines shoulder se draw karo. Ek line ko baar-baar scratch karke theek karne ki koshish mat karo.","modules":["m4"]},{"id":"ellipses","aliases":["how to draw ellipse","ellipse practice","circle looks wrong","draw circles","oval kaise banaye","ellipse kaise"],"keywords":["ellipse","ellipses","circle","oval","cylinder","ellipse","andaakar"],"en":"Ghost the ellipse first, then draw through it smoothly in one or two passes. Practise different degrees of tilt and width. Check whether the minor axis splits the ellipse symmetrically; avoid slowly tracing the outline.","hi":"Pehle ellipse ka motion ghost karo, phir ek-do smooth passes mein draw karo. Alag tilt aur width ke ellipses practise karo. Check karo ki minor axis ellipse ko symmetrically divide kar rahi hai ya nahi; outline ko dheere-dheere trace mat karo.","modules":["m4","m6","m10"]},{"id":"observation","aliases":["how to observe reference","draw what i see","drawing from reference","observation drawing","reference ko kaise dekhu","dekh kar draw"],"keywords":["observation","observe","reference","seeing","measure","compare","proportion","dekho"],"en":"Look for angles, negative spaces, proportions and large value groups instead of naming the object from memory. Compare relationships: how wide is one part relative to another, and where does an edge line up? Draw the specific shapes you see, not the symbol you expect.","hi":"Object ka naam sochne ke bajaye angles, negative spaces, proportions aur bade value groups dekho. Relationships compare karo: ek hissa doosre ke mukable kitna wide hai, aur edges kahan align hoti hain? Jo specific shapes dikh rahi hain wahi draw karo, memory wala generic symbol nahi.","modules":["m5","m6","m7"]},{"id":"shapes","aliases":["basic shapes drawing","draw shapes","shape construction","square circle triangle","basic shapes kaise","shape practice"],"keywords":["shape","shapes","circle","square","triangle","rectangle","construction"],"en":"Reduce complex subjects to simple 2D shapes first: circles, ovals, rectangles and triangles. Check their proportions and angles before adding detail. Shapes are the flat building blocks; forms are their 3D counterparts.","hi":"Complex subject ko pehle simple 2D shapes mein tod do: circles, ovals, rectangles aur triangles. Details add karne se pehle unke proportions aur angles check karo. Shapes flat building blocks hain; forms unke 3D versions hain.","modules":["m6","m10"]},{"id":"forms","aliases":["what are forms in drawing","shape vs form","3d forms","cube sphere cylinder","form drawing","shape aur form"],"keywords":["form","forms","3d","cube","sphere","cylinder","cone","shape"],"en":"A shape is flat; a form has volume and occupies 3D space. Practise spheres, boxes, cylinders and cones, then combine them to build objects. Add a centre line or cross-contour to show how the form turns in space.","hi":"Shape flat hoti hai; form mein volume hota hai aur woh 3D space occupy karti hai. Sphere, box, cylinder aur cone practise karo, phir inhe combine karke objects banao. Centre line ya cross-contour se dikhao ki form space mein kaise turn ho rahi hai.","modules":["m7","m10"]},{"id":"perspective","aliases":["what is perspective","one point perspective","two point perspective","vanishing point","horizon line","perspective kaise","vanishing point kya"],"keywords":["perspective","vanishing","horizon","one-point","two-point","foreshortening","depth"],"en":"Perspective is a system for showing 3D space on a flat page. In one-point perspective, receding parallel edges converge toward one vanishing point on the horizon; in two-point, they converge toward two points. Keep verticals consistent unless the viewpoint calls for them to tilt.","hi":"Perspective flat page par 3D space dikhane ka system hai. One-point perspective mein peeche jaati parallel edges horizon par ek vanishing point ki taraf milti hain; two-point mein do points hote hain. Vertical lines ko consistent rakho, jab tak viewpoint unhe tilt karne ki demand na kare.","modules":["m8","m10","m56"]},{"id":"gesture","aliases":["what is gesture drawing","gesture practice","dynamic pose","figure movement","gesture kaise draw","pose stiff"],"keywords":["gesture","pose","movement","action","dynamic","figure","stiff"],"en":"Gesture captures the action, direction and weight of a pose before anatomy or detail. Use a few flowing lines and simple masses; keep the study brief. Ask what the body is doing and where its weight is balanced.","hi":"Gesture pose ki action, direction aur weight capture karta hai—anatomy ya details se pehle. Kuch flowing lines aur simple masses use karo; study ko short rakho. Socho body kya action kar rahi hai aur weight kahan balance hai.","modules":["m9","m42","m45"]},{"id":"construction","aliases":["how to construct a drawing","construction method","draw from imagination","build object in 3d","drawing construction","imagination se draw"],"keywords":["construction","construct","build","imagination","structure","3d","forms"],"en":"Build the subject from simple volumes rather than copying its outer contour alone. Start with the largest masses, establish their orientation and overlap, then refine the silhouette and details. Construction helps the drawing hold together from different angles.","hi":"Sirf outer contour copy karne ke bajaye subject ko simple volumes se build karo. Sabse bade masses se shuru karo, unki direction aur overlap set karo, phir silhouette aur details refine karo. Construction se drawing alag angles par bhi believable rehti hai.","modules":["m10","m14","m41"]},{"id":"light-shadow","aliases":["how does light work in drawing","light and shadow","where to put shadows","shading logic","light source drawing","shadow kahan banaye","light shadow"],"keywords":["light","shadow","shading","highlight","cast","core","terminator","light source"],"en":"First identify the light source and the form’s orientation. Separate light family from shadow family: highlight, light, halftone, core shadow, reflected light and cast shadow. Keep the shadow family grouped instead of making every small area a different value.","hi":"Pehle light source aur form ki direction identify karo. Light family aur shadow family alag rakho: highlight, light, halftone, core shadow, reflected light aur cast shadow. Shadow side ko ek group ki tarah rakho; har chhote area ko alag value mat banao.","modules":["m11","m12"]},{"id":"shading","aliases":["how to shade","shading techniques","smooth shading","pencil shading","value scale","gradient shading","shade kaise kare","pencil se shading"],"keywords":["shade","shading","value","gradient","hatching","blending","tone","dark","light"],"en":"Build value gradually. Start with a simple value scale, keep pressure consistent, and layer strokes rather than pressing hard immediately. Use hatching or smooth transitions according to the surface; avoid smudging everything into one flat grey.","hi":"Values dheere-dheere build karo. Simple value scale se shuru karo, pressure consistent rakho aur turant hard press karne ke bajaye layers banao. Surface ke hisaab se hatching ya smooth transitions use karo; har cheez ko smudge karke ek flat grey mat bana do.","modules":["m12"]},{"id":"texture","aliases":["how to draw texture","texture techniques","hair texture","wood texture","stone texture","texture kaise banaye"],"keywords":["texture","surface","material","wood","stone","fabric","rough","smooth"],"en":"Texture should describe the surface, not become random decoration. Observe the scale, direction, spacing and contrast of the marks. Suggest texture with selective marks and let the underlying form remain readable.","hi":"Texture surface ko describe kare, random decoration na bane. Marks ka scale, direction, spacing aur contrast observe karo. Selective marks se texture suggest karo aur underlying form ko readable rehne do.","modules":["m13","m59","m65"]},{"id":"composition","aliases":["what is composition","how to compose drawing","rule of thirds","focal point","composition balance","composition kaise"],"keywords":["composition","focal","balance","framing","thumbnail","negative space","rule","thirds"],"en":"Composition is how you arrange shapes, values and empty space to guide the viewer. Start with small thumbnails, choose a clear focal point, and check the big light-dark pattern before rendering. Use negative space deliberately.","hi":"Composition ka matlab shapes, values aur empty space ko arrange karke viewer ki nazar guide karna hai. Chhote thumbnails se shuru karo, clear focal point chuno aur rendering se pehle bade light-dark pattern check karo. Negative space ko bhi consciously use karo.","modules":["m14","m79","m83"]},{"id":"proportion","aliases":["how to get proportions right","measure proportions","head proportions","body proportions","proportion drawing","proportion kaise"],"keywords":["proportion","measurement","ratio","scale","alignment","compare","anatomy"],"en":"Measure relationships rather than guessing isolated parts. Compare widths and heights, align landmarks, and check angles between key points. Re-check the whole drawing often; a local detail cannot fix a large proportion error.","hi":"Alag-alag parts ka andaaza lagane ke bajaye unke relationships measure karo. Width-height compare karo, landmarks align karo aur key points ke beech angles check karo. Puri drawing baar-baar recheck karo; chhoti detail bade proportion error ko fix nahi kar sakti.","modules":["m17","m28","m41"]},{"id":"head","aliases":["how to draw head","loomis method","head construction","draw face proportions","face kaise banaye","head kaise draw"],"keywords":["head","face","loomis","skull","portrait","proportions","jaw","cranium"],"en":"Begin with the cranium as a simple ball, then attach the jaw as a separate mass. Add the centre line and brow line to show the head’s tilt and rotation before placing features. Use the skull structure to guide the silhouette.","hi":"Cranium ko simple ball ki tarah banao, phir jaw ko alag mass ke roop mein attach karo. Features place karne se pehle centre line aur brow line se head ka tilt aur rotation dikhao. Silhouette guide karne ke liye skull structure samjho.","modules":["m15","m16","m18","m20"]},{"id":"eyes","aliases":["how to draw eyes","eye proportions","draw realistic eyes","eyes kaise banaye","eye drawing"],"keywords":["eye","eyes","eyeball","eyelid","iris","pupil","eyebrow"],"en":"Treat the eyeball as a sphere wrapped by upper and lower lids. The lids overlap the eyeball; they are not just almond outlines. Observe the opening, angle and thickness of each lid, then add iris and pupil with the same perspective as the eye.","hi":"Eyeball ko sphere samjho jise upper aur lower lids cover karte hain. Lids eyeball par overlap karti hain; woh sirf almond outline nahi hoti. Opening, angle aur lid ki thickness observe karo, phir iris aur pupil ko eye ki perspective ke hisaab se add karo.","modules":["m23","m24"]},{"id":"nose-mouth","aliases":["how to draw nose","how to draw mouth","nose construction","lips drawing","nose kaise banaye","mouth kaise draw"],"keywords":["nose","mouth","lips","nostril","philtrum","face feature"],"en":"Avoid outlining every feature with a dark contour. Build the nose from its bridge, tip, wings and underside planes; build the mouth around the muzzle and the cylinder of the teeth. Use value changes to describe form, not a symbol-like outline.","hi":"Har feature ko dark outline se mat banao. Nose ko bridge, tip, wings aur underside planes se build karo; mouth ko muzzle aur teeth ke cylinder ke around samjho. Form dikhane ke liye value changes use karo, symbol jaisi outline nahi.","modules":["m25","m26"]},{"id":"hands","aliases":["how to draw hands","hand anatomy","hand gestures","fingers proportions","hands kaise draw","fingers draw","haath kaise draw karu","haath kaise banaye","hands kaise draw karu"],"keywords":["hand","hands","finger","fingers","palm","knuckle","gesture"],"en":"Simplify the palm into a box-like mass and the fingers into linked segments. Establish the direction of the palm, the knuckle arc and the thumb placement before drawing individual fingers. Study the hand as a volume, not a flat symbol.","hi":"Palm ko box-like mass aur fingers ko linked segments mein simplify karo. Individual fingers draw karne se pehle palm ki direction, knuckle arc aur thumb placement set karo. Hand ko volume ki tarah study karo, flat symbol ki tarah nahi.","modules":["m36","m37"]},{"id":"anatomy","aliases":["how to learn anatomy for drawing","human anatomy drawing","muscles for artists","body anatomy","anatomy kaise seekhe"],"keywords":["anatomy","muscle","skeleton","bone","body","torso","limbs","structure"],"en":"Learn the skeleton and major masses before memorising small muscles. Understand how the rib cage, pelvis and limbs connect, then use simplified muscle groups to explain surface forms. Anatomy should support gesture and construction, not replace them.","hi":"Chhoti muscles yaad karne se pehle skeleton aur major masses samjho. Rib cage, pelvis aur limbs ka connection dekho, phir simplified muscle groups se surface forms explain karo. Anatomy gesture aur construction ko support kare, unki jagah na le.","modules":["m31","m34","m35","m41"]},{"id":"body-pose","aliases":["how to draw body pose","figure drawing","body movement","stiff pose","body proportions","figure kaise banaye"],"keywords":["body","figure","pose","movement","torso","pelvis","limbs","gesture"],"en":"Block the rib cage and pelvis as two large masses, connect them with the spine, then attach the limbs as simple cylinders. Check the line of action and weight balance before refining anatomy. Keep the pose readable at thumbnail size.","hi":"Rib cage aur pelvis ko do bade masses ki tarah block karo, spine se connect karo, phir limbs ko simple cylinders ki tarah attach karo. Anatomy refine karne se pehle line of action aur weight balance check karo. Pose chhote thumbnail size par bhi readable honi chahiye.","modules":["m34","m38","m41","m42"]},{"id":"hair","aliases":["how to draw hair","hair strands","hair volume","hair drawing","baal kaise draw"],"keywords":["hair","strands","locks","volume","hairstyle","baal"],"en":"Draw hair as grouped masses first, following the direction of growth and flow. Establish the outer silhouette and major light-dark groups before adding a few selective strands. Individual lines alone make hair look stringy and flat.","hi":"Hair ko pehle grouped masses ki tarah draw karo, growth aur flow ki direction follow karte hue. Kuch selected strands add karne se pehle outer silhouette aur major light-dark groups set karo. Sirf individual lines se hair stringy aur flat lagta hai.","modules":["m31"]},{"id":"clothing","aliases":["how to draw clothes","fabric folds","cloth wrinkles","clothing folds drawing","kapde ki folds"],"keywords":["clothing","fabric","fold","folds","wrinkle","cloth","drape"],"en":"Folds form because fabric is pulled, compressed or hanging under gravity. Find the tension points first, then group folds by their cause: pipe, zigzag, spiral or half-lock. Avoid drawing random wrinkle lines everywhere.","hi":"Fabric folds tab banti hain jab kapda pull, compress ya gravity se hang hota hai. Pehle tension points dhoondo, phir folds ko unke cause ke hisaab se group karo: pipe, zigzag, spiral ya half-lock. Har jagah random wrinkle lines mat banao.","modules":["m44"]},{"id":"animals","aliases":["how to draw animals","animal anatomy","quadruped drawing","animal skeleton","animals kaise draw"],"keywords":["animal","animals","quadruped","skeleton","gait","predator","bird","creature"],"en":"Start with the animal’s major masses and its centre of gravity. Study the skeleton and how the legs support weight; then add muscle masses and silhouette. Compare species rather than giving every animal the same generic body.","hi":"Animal ke major masses aur centre of gravity se shuru karo. Skeleton aur legs weight kaise support karti hain, yeh study karo; phir muscle masses aur silhouette add karo. Har animal ko ek hi generic body dene ke bajaye species ke differences compare karo.","modules":["m67","m68","m69","m70","m71","m72","m73","m74","m75","m76"]},{"id":"trees-nature","aliases":["how to draw trees","plants and foliage","tree structure","leaves drawing","trees kaise banaye"],"keywords":["tree","trees","plant","foliage","leaves","branches","canopy","nature"],"en":"Build the trunk and branching structure first. Group foliage into large canopy masses and vary their size, spacing and overlap; add selective leaf detail only where it helps explain the form. Avoid drawing hundreds of identical leaves.","hi":"Pehle trunk aur branching structure banao. Foliage ko bade canopy masses mein group karo aur unka size, spacing aur overlap vary karo; leaf details sirf wahan add karo jahan form samajhne mein help mile. Ek jaise hazaar leaves mat banao.","modules":["m48","m49","m50"]},{"id":"architecture","aliases":["how to draw buildings","architectural perspective","draw room interior","building perspective","building kaise draw"],"keywords":["architecture","building","interior","room","street","roof","window","door","perspective"],"en":"Begin with a perspective box that establishes the building’s overall volume. Keep edges aligned to the correct vanishing points, then subdivide the box for doors, windows and roof details. Add materials and wear after the structure reads clearly.","hi":"Building ka overall volume set karne ke liye perspective box se shuru karo. Edges ko sahi vanishing points ke saath align rakho, phir doors, windows aur roof details ke liye box subdivide karo. Structure clear hone ke baad materials aur wear add karo.","modules":["m56","m57","m58","m61","m63"]},{"id":"color-theory","aliases":["how to use color","color theory basics","color harmony","complementary colors","colour palette","colors kaise use"],"keywords":["color","colour","hue","saturation","value","palette","complementary","harmony"],"en":"Think about value, hue and saturation separately. Choose a limited palette, decide the dominant color relationship, and check that the value structure still reads in grayscale. Color cannot rescue unclear values or composition.","hi":"Value, hue aur saturation ko alag-alag samjho. Limited palette chuno, dominant color relationship decide karo aur grayscale mein bhi value structure check karo. Color unclear values ya composition ko rescue nahi kar sakta.","modules":["m80","m81","m82"]},{"id":"digital-start","aliases":["how to start digital art","digital drawing beginner","drawing tablet needed","digital art software","digital art kaise shuru"],"keywords":["digital","tablet","software","stylus","app","procreate","krita","photoshop"],"en":"Digital art still uses the same drawing fundamentals. Start with a simple app and a basic brush; learn canvas navigation, layers, undo and export before exploring advanced effects. A tablet is useful, but it does not replace observation or construction practice.","hi":"Digital art mein bhi wahi drawing fundamentals kaam aate hain. Simple app aur basic brush se shuru karo; advanced effects se pehle canvas navigation, layers, undo aur export seekho. Tablet useful hai, lekin observation aur construction practice ki jagah nahi leta.","modules":["m87","m88","m89"]},{"id":"layers","aliases":["what are layers","how to use layers","layers in digital art","layer blending modes","digital layers kya"],"keywords":["layer","layers","blend","opacity","mask","digital","stack"],"en":"Layers separate parts of an artwork so you can edit them independently. Keep sketches, line work, flats, shadows and effects on separate layers when that helps your workflow. Name important layers and avoid creating dozens without a reason.","hi":"Layers artwork ke parts ko alag rakhti hain, taaki unhe independently edit kar sako. Workflow mein help mile toh sketch, line work, flats, shadows aur effects alag layers par rakho. Important layers ko name do; bina reason dozens layers mat banao.","modules":["m90","m91","m92"]},{"id":"brushes","aliases":["which brush should i use","digital brushes","brush settings","brush size opacity","brush kaunsa use kare"],"keywords":["brush","brushes","settings","size","opacity","hardness","texture"],"en":"Start with one simple round brush and learn its size, opacity and pressure behaviour. Add textured or specialised brushes only when you know what problem they solve. A large brush library does not automatically improve the artwork.","hi":"Ek simple round brush se shuru karo aur uska size, opacity aur pressure behaviour samjho. Textured ya specialised brushes tab add karo jab pata ho ki woh kaunsi problem solve karte hain. Bahut saare brushes hone se artwork automatically better nahi hota.","modules":["m87","m88","m93"]},{"id":"resolution","aliases":["what resolution should i use","canvas size dpi ppi","image resolution","print resolution","dpi kya hota"],"keywords":["resolution","dpi","ppi","pixels","canvas","print","300","pixel"],"en":"For screen artwork, choose pixel dimensions suited to the final display. For print, ask the printer for specifications; 300 PPI at final print size is a common target, but it is not a universal rule. Keep the original file so you can export different sizes later.","hi":"Screen artwork ke liye final display ke hisaab se pixel dimensions chuno. Print ke liye printer ki specifications lo; final print size par 300 PPI common target hai, lekin universal rule nahi. Original file sambhal kar rakho, taaki baad mein alag sizes export kar sako.","modules":["m94","m130"]},{"id":"export","aliases":["how to export artwork","png or jpg","export settings","save drawing file","file format","png jpg difference"],"keywords":["export","save","png","jpg","jpeg","file","format","transparent"],"en":"Keep an editable working file, then export a copy for sharing. PNG is useful for crisp graphics or transparency; JPEG is commonly used for photos and smaller files but uses lossy compression. Check dimensions and colour appearance after export.","hi":"Editable working file sambhal kar rakho, phir sharing ke liye copy export karo. PNG crisp graphics ya transparency ke liye useful hai; JPEG photos aur chhoti files ke liye common hai, lekin lossy compression use karta hai. Export ke baad dimensions aur colors check karo.","modules":["m95","m130"]},{"id":"non-destructive","aliases":["what is non destructive workflow","layers masks adjustment","destructive editing","non destructive editing","flatten image"],"keywords":["non-destructive","destructive","mask","adjustment","flatten","editable","workflow"],"en":"A non-destructive workflow preserves the ability to revise decisions. Use layers, masks, adjustment layers and smart objects where available instead of permanently erasing or flattening too early. Keep a clean source file and export flattened copies only when needed.","hi":"Non-destructive workflow mein tum apne decisions baad mein revise kar sakte ho. Jahan possible ho layers, masks, adjustment layers aur smart objects use karo; jaldi permanently erase ya flatten mat karo. Clean source file rakho aur zaroorat par hi flattened copy export karo.","modules":["m105","m111"]},{"id":"composition-concept","aliases":["how to make concept art","concept art process","thumbnailing","visual development","concept art kaise"],"keywords":["concept","thumbnail","iteration","brief","visual development","design"],"en":"Start from the brief: identify the subject, purpose, audience and constraints. Make several small thumbnails with genuinely different compositions, choose the clearest direction, then refine values, lighting and details. Do not polish the first idea before exploring alternatives.","hi":"Brief se shuru karo: subject, purpose, audience aur constraints samjho. Kai chhote thumbnails banao jinki compositions sach mein alag hon, sabse clear direction chuno, phir values, lighting aur details refine karo. Alternatives explore kiye bina pehle idea ko polish mat karo.","modules":["m83","m84","m85"]},{"id":"character-design","aliases":["how to design a character","character design process","silhouette design","character sheet","character kaise design"],"keywords":["character","design","silhouette","turnaround","expression","props","brief"],"en":"Define the character’s role, personality and context before drawing. Explore distinct silhouettes in thumbnails, then refine the chosen design with proportions, costume, expressions and props. Test whether the character reads clearly without a written explanation.","hi":"Draw karne se pehle character ka role, personality aur context define karo. Thumbnails mein alag silhouettes explore karo, phir proportions, costume, expressions aur props refine karo. Check karo ki bina written explanation ke bhi character samajh aa raha hai ya nahi.","modules":["m46","m121"]},{"id":"storyboard","aliases":["what is storyboard","how to draw storyboard","storyboard panels","animatic meaning","storyboard kaise","what is animatic","what is an animatic","animatic kya hoti hai"],"keywords":["storyboard","panel","animatic","shot","sequence","pitch","timing"],"en":"A storyboard plans a sequence of shots and actions; it is a communication tool, not a finished illustration. Focus on staging, camera, clear action and emotional beats. An animatic edits storyboard panels with timing and sound so pacing can be tested before full animation.","hi":"Storyboard shots aur actions ki sequence plan karta hai; yeh communication tool hai, finished illustration nahi. Staging, camera, clear action aur emotional beats par focus karo. Animatic panels ko timing aur sound ke saath edit karta hai, taaki full animation se pehle pacing test ho sake.","modules":["m116","m129"]},{"id":"portfolio","aliases":["how to make art portfolio","artist portfolio","portfolio pieces","art portfolio beginner","portfolio kaise banaye","portfolio kaise banau","art portfolio kaise banaye","portfolio banana kaise shuru karu"],"keywords":["portfolio","career","pieces","presentation","selection","artstation"],"en":"Choose a small set of your strongest, relevant work rather than uploading everything. Show process where it helps: sketches, iterations and final outcomes. Tailor the portfolio to the role or audience, and make contact details and project context easy to find.","hi":"Har cheez upload karne ke bajaye apne strongest aur relevant kaam ka chhota selection rakho. Jahan useful ho process dikhao: sketches, iterations aur final result. Portfolio ko target role ya audience ke hisaab se tailor karo, aur project context clear rakho.","modules":["m114","m120"]},{"id":"practice-routine","aliases":["how often should i practice drawing","daily drawing practice","practice routine","how long to draw","practice kitni der"],"keywords":["practice","routine","daily","hours","consistency","habit","schedule"],"en":"A consistent, focused session is more useful than occasional marathon sessions. Pick one clear goal for each session, warm up briefly, practise that skill, then review one thing to improve next time. Rest when tired; quality of attention matters more than a huge hour count.","hi":"Kabhi-kabhi bahut lambi session se better hai consistent focused practice. Har session ka ek clear goal rakho, short warm-up karo, skill practise karo aur end mein ek cheez note karo jo next time improve karni hai. Thakne par rest lo; attention ki quality hours ki badi sankhya se zyada matter karti hai.","modules":["m1","m4","m7"]},{"id":"mistakes","aliases":["why my drawing looks wrong","how to improve drawing","common drawing mistakes","drawing not improving","drawing galat lagti"],"keywords":["mistake","wrong","improve","stuck","bad","problem","error"],"en":"Do not add more detail immediately. Step back and check the largest issues first: proportion, angle, perspective, value grouping and silhouette. Compare against the reference, identify one specific mismatch, and correct that before polishing.","hi":"Turant aur details add mat karo. Peeche hatkar sabse bade issues check karo: proportion, angle, perspective, value grouping aur silhouette. Reference se compare karo, ek specific mismatch identify karo aur polish karne se pehle use correct karo.","modules":["m4","m5","m6","m7"]},{"id":"reference-use","aliases":["can i copy reference","using references","photo reference drawing","is tracing cheating","reference use karna"],"keywords":["reference","copy","trace","photo","study","cheating"],"en":"References are useful tools for studying shape, light, anatomy and material. The important part is to observe and understand what you copy, not just reproduce marks blindly. For portfolio or public work, respect the source and follow its licence; do not present someone else’s work as yours.","hi":"References shape, light, anatomy aur material study karne ke useful tools hain. Zaroori baat yeh hai ki jo copy kar rahe ho use observe aur understand karo, blindly marks reproduce nahi. Portfolio ya public work mein source ka respect karo, licence follow karo aur kisi aur ka kaam apna mat batao.","modules":["m5","m7","m111"]},{"id":"negative-space","aliases":["what is negative space","negative space drawing","draw around object","empty space composition","negative space kya"],"keywords":["negative","space","empty","gap","silhouette","composition"],"en":"Negative space is the empty area around and between objects. Compare its shape just like you compare the object itself; it often reveals proportion and alignment errors quickly. Use it to balance a composition and clarify the silhouette.","hi":"Negative space objects ke aas-paas aur unke beech ki khaali jagah hoti hai. Uski shape ko bhi object ki tarah compare karo; isse proportion aur alignment ki galti jaldi pakad mein aati hai. Composition balance aur silhouette clear karne ke liye bhi use karo.","modules":["m5","m14","m79"]},{"id":"foreshortening","aliases":["what is foreshortening","draw arm toward camera","foreshortened figure","foreshortening kaise"],"keywords":["foreshortening","foreshorten","camera","depth","overlap","perspective","limb"],"en":"Foreshortening happens when a form points toward or away from the viewer, making its apparent length shorter. Use overlapping masses, clear axis direction and perspective to show depth. Measure the visible shape rather than relying on what you know the limb’s full length to be.","hi":"Foreshortening tab hoti hai jab form viewer ki taraf ya usse door point karti hai, jis se uski apparent length chhoti dikhti hai. Depth dikhane ke liye overlapping masses, clear axis direction aur perspective use karo. Limb ki actual length ke andaaze ke bajaye jo visible shape hai use measure karo.","modules":["m43"]},{"id":"lighting-concept","aliases":["how to design lighting","mood atmosphere","color scripting","dramatic lighting art","lighting kaise"],"keywords":["lighting","mood","atmosphere","color script","rim light","key light","environment"],"en":"Decide what the light is doing for the scene: time, mood, focus and readability. Establish the main light direction and broad value pattern first, then use colour temperature and selective accents. Keep the focal area clear instead of making every part equally bright.","hi":"Scene mein light ka purpose decide karo: time, mood, focus aur readability. Pehle main light direction aur broad value pattern set karo, phir colour temperature aur selected accents use karo. Har part ko equally bright banane ke bajaye focal area clear rakho.","modules":["m80","m81","m82"]},{"id":"digital-color","aliases":["how to color digital painting","flat colors shading digital","coloring workflow","digital painting color"],"keywords":["coloring","flats","shading","digital","paint","color","colour"],"en":"Separate the colour workflow into clear stages: flats first, then shadow and light decisions, then material and edge refinements. Keep values readable and use layers or masks so you can adjust colour without repainting everything.","hi":"Colour workflow ko clear stages mein baanto: pehle flats, phir shadow aur light decisions, phir material aur edge refinements. Values readable rakho aur layers ya masks use karo, taaki sab kuch dobara paint kiye bina colour adjust kar sako.","modules":["m90","m92","m93"]},{"id":"webtoon-comic","aliases":["how to make comic","comic panels","webtoon scroll format","manga page layout","comic kaise banaye"],"keywords":["comic","manga","webtoon","panel","gutter","page","sequential"],"en":"Plan the reading flow before polishing individual panels. Use panel size, spacing and composition to control pacing; in vertical scroll formats, the gap between panels affects timing. Make speech balloons readable and guide the eye clearly through the sequence.","hi":"Individual panels polish karne se pehle reading flow plan karo. Panel size, spacing aur composition se pacing control karo; vertical scroll format mein panels ke beech ka gap timing ko affect karta hai. Speech balloons readable rakho aur viewer ki nazar ko sequence mein clearly guide karo.","modules":["m116","m117","m118","m125"]},{"id":"digital-composite","aliases":["how to make photo composite","compositing realism","match lighting composite","photo manipulation"],"keywords":["composite","compositing","mask","lighting","perspective","shadow","match"],"en":"A believable composite depends on matching perspective, scale, lighting direction, colour temperature, sharpness and grain. Match the light before spending time perfecting the mask edge. Add contact and cast shadows so the subject sits in the scene.","hi":"Believable composite ke liye perspective, scale, light direction, colour temperature, sharpness aur grain match hone chahiye. Mask edge perfect karne se pehle lighting match karo. Contact aur cast shadows add karo, taaki subject scene mein properly sit kare.","modules":["m112","m113"]},{"id":"3d-basics","aliases":["how to use 3d in art","3d blockout","3d reference drawing","3d model for concept art"],"keywords":["3d","blockout","model","camera","render","reference","perspective"],"en":"Use simple 3D blockouts to check camera, perspective and large forms, not as a substitute for design decisions. Keep the model simple, choose a useful view, and paint or draw over it where artistic judgement is needed.","hi":"Simple 3D blockouts ko camera, perspective aur large forms check karne ke liye use karo, design decisions ki jagah nahi. Model simple rakho, useful view chuno aur jahan artistic judgement chahiye wahan paint ya draw over karo.","modules":["m109","m110","m112"]},{"id":"print-production","aliases":["how to prepare art for print","bleed crop marks print","print file setup","artwork printing"],"keywords":["print","bleed","crop","marks","cmyk","resolution","dpi","paper"],"en":"Prepare artwork to the printer’s specifications. Confirm final dimensions, bleed, safe area, colour mode, resolution and file format before export. Ask the printer for a template when possible; different print processes have different requirements.","hi":"Artwork ko printer ki specifications ke hisaab se prepare karo. Export se pehle final dimensions, bleed, safe area, colour mode, resolution aur file format confirm karo. Possible ho toh printer se template lo; alag print processes ki requirements alag hoti hain.","modules":["m130"]},{"id":"feedback-critique","aliases":["how to critique my art","get feedback","art critique","how to review drawing","feedback kaise le"],"keywords":["feedback","critique","review","improve","self-check","analysis"],"en":"Ask for feedback on a specific question instead of asking only “is it good?” For example: does the pose read, is the focal point clear, or are the values grouped? Review the answer, choose one change, and test it in the next iteration.","hi":"Sirf “achha hai?” poochne ke bajaye specific feedback maango. Jaise: pose clear hai, focal point samajh aa raha hai, ya values sahi group hain? Feedback samjho, ek change chuno aur next iteration mein test karo.","modules":["m1","m7","m83"]},{"id":"artist-block","aliases":["i have art block","no motivation to draw","cant think of ideas","artist block help","drawing ka mann nahi"],"keywords":["block","motivation","ideas","stuck","inspiration","bored","blank"],"en":"Lower the task size rather than waiting for inspiration. Do a five-minute observation study, copy a simple object from life for practice, or make ten tiny thumbnails without judging them. If you are tired, take a break and return with one small goal.","hi":"Inspiration ka wait karne ke bajaye task chhota karo. Five-minute observation study karo, life se ek simple object practise ke liye draw karo, ya bina judge kiye ten tiny thumbnails banao. Thake hue ho toh break lo aur ek chhote goal ke saath wapas aao.","modules":["m1","m4","m5","m83"]},{"id":"art-career","aliases":["how to become concept artist","art career skills","freelance artist","artist job portfolio","artist career"],"keywords":["career","concept artist","freelance","job","studio","industry","client"],"en":"Build fundamentals first, then develop a focused body of work for the role you want. Study professional briefs and pipelines, practise presenting your decisions, and learn to revise from feedback. A portfolio should show relevant problem-solving, not just attractive finished images.","hi":"Pehle fundamentals build karo, phir target role ke liye focused body of work banao. Professional briefs aur pipelines study karo, apne decisions present karna seekho aur feedback ke hisaab se revise karo. Portfolio mein sirf attractive finished images nahi, relevant problem-solving bhi dikhna chahiye.","modules":["m120","m121","m122","m123"]},{"id":"materials-alternatives","aliases":["i have no art supplies","no art supplies","mujhe art supplies nahi hai","art supplies nahi hai","no sketchbook what to do","cheap drawing tools","can i use notebook","materials nahi hai"],"keywords":["no supplies","supplies","cheap","notebook","copy","paper","pencil","budget","tools nahi"],"en":"Use what you already have: an ordinary pencil, notebook or loose paper, and a basic eraser if available. You can practise observation, shapes, lines and gesture without specialist supplies. Focus on the exercise, not on buying a perfect setup.","hi":"Jo already paas hai wahi use karo: normal pencil, notebook ya loose paper, aur agar ho toh basic eraser. Observation, shapes, lines aur gesture bina specialist supplies ke practise ho sakte hain. Perfect setup kharidne ke bajaye exercise par focus karo.","modules":["m2","m4","m5"]},{"id":"why-practice","aliases":["why do i need boring drills","line drills boring","fundamentals boring","why practice basics"],"keywords":["boring","drill","fundamentals","basics","practice","skip"],"en":"Fundamental drills isolate one skill so you can notice and correct it. They may feel repetitive, but they build control that later makes complex subjects easier. Keep drills short and connect them to a drawing you actually want to make.","hi":"Fundamental drills ek skill ko alag karke practise karwate hain, taaki tum use notice aur correct kar sako. Repetitive lag sakte hain, lekin wahi control baad mein complex subjects easy banata hai. Drills short rakho aur unhe kisi aisi drawing se connect karo jo tum banana chahte ho.","modules":["m1","m4","m6"]},{"id":"difference-pixel-vector","aliases":["difference between raster and vector","pixel vs vector art","vector drawing meaning","raster art"],"keywords":["raster","vector","pixel","pixels","paths","svg","bitmap"],"en":"Raster artwork is made of pixels, so enlarging it too much can reveal pixelation. Vector artwork is built from paths and shapes that can scale cleanly. Use raster for painterly images and texture; use vector when crisp scalable shapes and graphics matter.","hi":"Raster artwork pixels se banta hai, isliye bahut enlarge karne par pixels dikh sakte hain. Vector artwork paths aur shapes se banta hai jo cleanly scale ho sakte hain. Painterly images aur texture ke liye raster; crisp scalable graphics ke liye vector useful hai.","modules":["m87","m94"]},{"id":"unknown-topic","aliases":["something else","help me","i have a question"],"keywords":["help","question","doubt","explain","samjhao","batao"],"en":"I could not confidently match that to a prepared answer. Try naming the topic and the specific thing you want to know—for example, “how do I shade a sphere?”, “why do my proportions look wrong?”, or “what is a vanishing point?”. I can also point you to the closest lessons below.","hi":"Is sawaal ko main kisi prepared answer se confidently match nahi kar paaya. Topic aur exact doubt batao—jaise “sphere ko shade kaise karun?”, “proportions galat kyun lagte hain?” ya “vanishing point kya hota hai?”. Neeche closest lessons bhi dekh sakte ho.","modules":[]},{"id":"value-study","aliases":["what is a value study","how to make value thumbnails","grayscale value study","value grouping","value study kaise kare"],"keywords":["value study","grayscale","thumbnail","value","light dark","tonal"],"en":"A value study reduces an image to a few light-to-dark groups before full rendering. Try three values first—light, middle and dark—so you can judge the composition and focal point without getting distracted by colour or detail. If it reads clearly in three values, you can add more subtle transitions later.","hi":"Value study mein full rendering se pehle image ko kuch light aur dark groups mein simplify karte hain. Pehle sirf teen values try karo—light, midtone aur dark—taaki colour aur details mein uljhe bina composition aur focal point check kar sako. Agar image teen values mein clear lagti hai, toh baad mein subtle transitions add karna.","modules":["m92","m99"]},{"id":"curves-levels","aliases":["what are curves and levels","how to use curves adjustment","curves vs levels","s curve color grading","curves kaise use kare"],"keywords":["curves","levels","adjustment","s-curve","contrast","color grade"],"en":"Levels mainly adjusts the black point, white point and midpoint. Curves lets you add several control points across the tonal range, so you can shape shadows, midtones and highlights more precisely. Use an adjustment layer so the change stays editable.","hi":"Levels mainly black point, white point aur midpoint control karta hai. Curves mein tonal range par kai control points add kar sakte ho, isliye shadows, midtones aur highlights ko zyada precisely adjust kar paate ho. Adjustment layer use karo, taaki change baad mein bhi edit ho sake.","modules":["m112"]},{"id":"photobashing","aliases":["what is photobashing","how to photobash","photobashing workflow","use photos in concept art","photobash kaise kare"],"keywords":["photobash","photobashing","photo","concept art","reference","cutout"],"en":"Photobashing combines photographic elements with painted or drawn work to explore or build a concept quickly. Match perspective, scale, lighting direction and colour temperature first; then integrate edges, texture and paint-over so the result feels like one coherent image. Check image rights before using photos in public or client work.","hi":"Photobashing mein photos ke elements ko painting ya drawing ke saath combine karke concept jaldi explore ya build karte hain. Sabse pehle perspective, scale, light direction aur colour temperature match karo; phir edges, texture aur paint-over se sabko ek hi coherent image jaisa banao. Public ya client work mein photos use karne se pehle unke usage rights check karo.","modules":["m113"]},{"id":"compositing","aliases":["how to make a realistic composite","photo compositing tips","why does my composite look fake","composite lighting match"],"keywords":["composite","compositing","mask","contact shadow","cast shadow","grain","sharpness","light match"],"en":"A convincing composite needs more than a clean cutout. Match perspective, scale, light direction, colour temperature, sharpness and grain. Add contact and cast shadows so the subject belongs in the scene, and judge the whole image at normal viewing size.","hi":"Believable composite ke liye sirf clean cutout kaafi nahi hota. Perspective, scale, light direction, colour temperature, sharpness aur grain match karo. Contact aur cast shadows add karo, taaki subject scene ka hissa lage. Puri image ko normal viewing size par bhi check karo.","modules":["m112","m113","m118"]},{"id":"master-study","aliases":["how to do a master study","copy old master paintings","master study method","study another artist artwork","master studies","how to do master studies","master study kaise kare"],"keywords":["master study","master","artist study","copy","analyse","reference"],"en":"Before copying a masterwork, choose one question to investigate—such as value grouping, edge control, colour harmony or brushwork. Study a small section, identify how the artist solved that problem, then apply the finding to an original subject. Copying without a learning goal often produces imitation without transferable understanding.","hi":"Kisi masterwork ko copy karne se pehle ek sawaal chuno—jaise value grouping, edge control, colour harmony ya brushwork. Chhote section ko study karo, samjho artist ne woh problem kaise solve ki, phir us learning ko apne original subject par apply karo. Bina clear goal ke copying se imitation toh hoti hai, lekin transferable understanding kam milti hai.","modules":["m117"]},{"id":"speed-painting","aliases":["how to speed paint","speed painting workflow","paint faster","timed painting practice"],"keywords":["speed paint","speed painting","time limit","thumbnail","block in","workflow"],"en":"Speed painting is about making clear decisions quickly, not rushing every brushstroke. Work from large shapes to smaller ones: establish composition and value masses, set the light direction, then add only the details that strengthen the read. Use a timer to practise prioritising, not to judge your worth as an artist.","hi":"Speed painting ka matlab har brushstroke jaldi karna nahi, balki clear decisions jaldi lena hai. Bade shapes se chhoti details ki taraf jao: pehle composition aur value masses set karo, light direction decide karo, phir sirf wahi details add karo jo image ko stronger banati hain. Timer ko priorities practise karne ke liye use karo, apni ability judge karne ke liye nahi.","modules":["m116"]},{"id":"edge-control","aliases":["what is edge control in painting","hard soft lost edges","how to use edges","edge variety drawing"],"keywords":["edge","edges","hard edge","soft edge","lost edge","found edge","focus"],"en":"Edges describe how sharply one shape meets another. Hard edges attract attention; soft edges suggest gradual transitions; lost edges let adjacent values merge. Use the sharpest edges near the focal area and vary edge softness to guide the viewer rather than outlining everything equally.","hi":"Edges batati hain ki ek shape doosri se kitni sharply milti hai. Hard edges nazar kheenchti hain; soft edges gradual transition dikhati hain; lost edges mein paas-paas ki values merge ho jaati hain. Focal area ke paas sharpest edges rakho aur baaki jagah edge softness vary karo—har cheez ko equally outline mat karo.","modules":["m96"]},{"id":"editorial-illustration","aliases":["how to make editorial illustration","what is editorial art","illustrate an article","editorial illustration brief"],"keywords":["editorial","illustration","article","brief","metaphor","visual idea"],"en":"Editorial illustration turns an article’s central idea into a clear visual metaphor. Identify the main argument, audience and tone, then sketch several distinct concepts before choosing one. The image should communicate quickly at the size it will actually appear, not depend on a long explanation.","hi":"Editorial illustration kisi article ke main idea ko ek clear visual metaphor mein badalti hai. Pehle article ka central point, audience aur tone samjho; phir ek idea choose karne se pehle kai alag concepts ke quick sketches banao. Image us actual size par bhi jaldi samajh aani chahiye jahan woh publish hogi—use samjhane ke liye lambi explanation nahi lagni chahiye.","modules":["m121"]},{"id":"comic-lettering","aliases":["how to letter comics","comic lettering rules","speech bubble placement","comic speech balloons"],"keywords":["lettering","balloon","speech bubble","comic","font","reading order","tail"],"en":"Comic lettering is part of the storytelling. Keep text readable, choose a type size that works at the final page size, and place balloons in the order the reader should follow. Balloon tails should point clearly to the speaker without crossing important art or confusing the panel flow.","hi":"Comic lettering bhi storytelling ka hissa hai. Text readable rakho, final page size par sahi dikhne wala type size chuno aur speech balloons ko us order mein place karo jisme reader ko padhna hai. Balloon tails clearly speaker ki taraf point karein aur important artwork ya panel flow ko confuse na karein.","modules":["m123"]},{"id":"manga-reading","aliases":["which direction to read manga","manga page reading order","right to left manga","manga reading direction"],"keywords":["manga","right to left","reading order","panel order","gutter"],"en":"Traditional Japanese manga is generally read right to left, including panel order and speech balloons. Follow the reading direction consistently so the page flow stays clear. If you are creating a work for a different audience, decide the reading direction early and design the layout around it.","hi":"Traditional Japanese manga aam taur par right to left padhi jaati hai—panel order aur speech balloons bhi isi direction mein hote hain. Reading direction consistently follow karo, taaki page ka flow clear rahe. Agar tum kisi aur audience ke liye kaam bana rahe ho, toh direction pehle decide karo aur layout usi hisaab se design karo.","modules":["m124"]},{"id":"webtoon-layout","aliases":["how to layout a webtoon","vertical scroll comic pacing","webtoon panel spacing","webtoon gutters"],"keywords":["webtoon","vertical scroll","scroll","panel spacing","gutter","pacing"],"en":"In a vertical-scroll comic, the space between panels controls timing as well as separation. A larger gap can create a pause or reveal; a tighter gap can make events feel connected and quick. Test the page on a phone-sized screen because that is how most readers will experience it.","hi":"Vertical-scroll comic mein panels ke beech ki khaali jagah sirf separation nahi, timing bhi control karti hai. Bada gap pause ya reveal create kar sakta hai; chhota gap events ko connected aur fast feel kara sakta hai. Page ko phone-size screen par test karo, kyunki zyada tar readers use isi tarah dekhenge.","modules":["m125"]},{"id":"environment-storytelling","aliases":["how to tell stories through environment","environmental storytelling","world building through props","show story in background"],"keywords":["environmental storytelling","world building","props","history","environment","story"],"en":"Environmental storytelling communicates history and culture through spaces, objects, wear and arrangement. Ask who uses the place, what happened there and what evidence remains. Let props and environmental details support the story instead of adding decoration without a reason.","hi":"Environmental storytelling spaces, objects, wear aur unki arrangement ke through history aur culture dikhati hai. Socho is jagah ka use kaun karta hai, yahan kya hua hoga aur uske kya signs bache hain. Props aur environment details ko story support karne do; bina reason decoration mat jodo.","modules":["m78","m85"]},{"id":"visual-development","aliases":["what is visual development","visdev meaning","visual development pipeline","define a visual style for a project"],"keywords":["visual development","visdev","style guide","mood","palette","project look"],"en":"Visual development defines the project’s overall visual language before full production: shape language, colour palette, lighting mood, character style and environment tone. It is a consistent system for the whole project, not just one attractive illustration. Use style guides and visual tests to keep the team aligned.","hi":"Visual development full production se pehle project ki overall visual language define karti hai: shape language, colour palette, lighting mood, character style aur environment ka tone. Yeh poore project ke liye ek consistent system hota hai, sirf ek sundar illustration nahi. Team ko aligned rakhne ke liye style guide aur visual tests use karo.","modules":["m126"]},{"id":"game-art-pipeline","aliases":["what is game art pipeline","how does concept art become game asset","what is retopology","what are uv maps","what is lod in games"],"keywords":["game art","pipeline","retopology","uv","bake","rigging","lod","polygon","engine","asset"],"en":"A typical game-art pipeline moves from concept and reference to blockout, high-detail sculpt, retopology, UVs, baking, texturing, rigging and engine import. LODs provide simpler versions for smaller on-screen objects, reducing rendering cost. Ask about the target platform and performance budget early; the best asset balances visual quality with what the game can run.","hi":"Typical game-art pipeline concept aur reference se shuru hoti hai, phir blockout, high-detail sculpt, retopology, UVs, baking, texturing, rigging aur engine import tak jaati hai. LODs chhote dikhne wale objects ke liye simpler versions deti hain, jisse rendering cost kam hoti hai. Shuru mein hi target platform aur performance budget samjho; best asset wahi hai jo visual quality aur game ki performance dono balance kare.","modules":["m128"]},{"id":"animation-preproduction","aliases":["what happens before animation","animation pre production","what is animatic workflow","animation storyboard process","what is animatic","what is an animatic","animatic kya hoti hai","animatic meaning"],"keywords":["animation","pre-production","storyboard","animatic","script","timing","casting"],"en":"Animation pre-production tests the story before full animation becomes expensive. Storyboards plan shots, staging and action; an animatic edits those panels with timing and sound so the team can judge pacing. Revisions at this stage are much cheaper than rebuilding finished animation.","hi":"Animation pre-production mein full animation shuru hone se pehle story test ki jaati hai, jab changes karna sasta hota hai. Storyboards shots, staging aur action plan karte hain; animatic un panels ko timing aur sound ke saath edit karti hai, taaki team pacing judge kar sake. Is stage par revisions karna finished animation dobara banane se kaafi aasaan aur sasta hota hai.","modules":["m129"]},{"id":"color-scripting","aliases":["what is a color script","color script for animation","plan color mood across scenes","color progression story"],"keywords":["color script","colour script","color","mood","scene","sequence","animation"],"en":"A colour script maps the colour and lighting mood across key story moments. It helps the audience feel changes in time, emotion and narrative direction. Plan the emotional beats first, then choose palettes and value patterns that support each beat while keeping the whole sequence coherent.","hi":"Colour script story ke important moments mein colour aur lighting ka mood map karti hai. Isse audience ko time, emotion aur story direction ke changes feel hote hain. Pehle emotional beats plan karo, phir har beat ko support karne wali palette aur value patterns chuno, aur poori sequence ka visual flow consistent rakho.","modules":["m80","m126"]},{"id":"style-development","aliases":["how to develop my art style","find your art style","art style comes from practice","how to make style consistent"],"keywords":["style","art style","influence","consistency","personal style","master study"],"en":"An art style develops through repeated choices in shape, proportion, edges, colour and simplification. It is not something you need to force at the beginning. Study artists with a clear question, practise fundamentals, and notice which visual decisions you naturally return to across different subjects.","hi":"Art style shape, proportion, edges, colour aur simplification mein baar-baar liye gaye decisions se develop hoti hai. Shuru mein use force karne ki zaroorat nahi. Artists ko ek clear question ke saath study karo, fundamentals practise karo aur dekho ki alag subjects banate waqt tum kaunse visual choices naturally repeat karte ho.","modules":["m119"]},{"id":"art-brief","aliases":["how to read an art brief","write a design brief","what goes in a concept art brief","client brief questions"],"keywords":["brief","client","function","audience","constraints","references","negative reference"],"en":"A useful brief states the purpose, audience, function, context and constraints of the design. Collect positive references and, when helpful, negative references that show what to avoid. Clarify deliverables and technical limits before polishing a concept.","hi":"Achha brief design ka purpose, audience, function, context aur constraints clear karta hai. Positive references collect karo aur zaroorat ho toh negative references bhi rakho, jo dikhayein ki kya avoid karna hai. Concept polish karne se pehle deliverables aur technical limits clear kar lo.","modules":["m127","m128"]},{"id":"sphere-drawing","aliases":["how to draw a sphere","draw a sphere","sphere drawing","sphere ko kaise draw kare","sphere kaise banaye"],"keywords":["sphere","ball","form","cross contour"],"en":"Start with a light circle, then wrap it with a centre line or cross-contour to show its 3D direction. Check the ellipse of the contour as the sphere turns, and keep the outline simple. If you are shading it, identify the light source first and separate the light side from the shadow family.","hi":"Ek light circle se shuru karo, phir centre line ya cross-contour add karo taaki sphere ki 3D direction samajh aaye. Sphere turn ho raha ho toh contour ke ellipse ko check karo aur outline simple rakho. Agar shading karni hai, toh pehle light source identify karo aur light side ko shadow family se alag rakho.","modules":["m7","m10","m11","m12"]}]};
